+# Smart OpenConnect 0.2 UI preview - build status
+
+Base: official OpenConnect for Android 1.12 source (`net.openconnect_vpn.android`, GPLv2+).
+
+## Implemented in the working source
+
+- Separate test application ID: `net.openconnect_vpn.android.smart`.
+- App label: `Smart OpenConnect`; version `0.1.0-mvp1`.
+- Fixed bottom navigation: **Connect / Servers / Log**.
+- FAQ / Settings / SecurID / About remain available from the overflow menu, including on the Connect screen.
+- Primary **Connect / Disconnect** button is fixed in the lower thumb zone immediately above bottom navigation.
+- Server list tap now selects a profile and returns to Connect instead of connecting immediately.
+- Per-profile **Smart Relay** checkbox, default ON.
+- Dynamic Smart Relay discovery:
+  - system DNS for the selected hostname;
+  - Google and Cloudflare DNS-over-HTTPS views;
+  - relay addresses learned from other configured Keenetic/Netcraze profiles;
+  - persistent locally cached relay pool across connection attempts.
+- Relay health probing in parallel using TCP + TLS with the original logical hostname as SNI.
+- Fastest TLS-healthy relay selected before OpenConnect authentication.
+- Native libopenconnect `getaddrinfo()` override pins the physical relay IP while preserving the original hostname for SNI / certificate processing / HTTP Host.
+- Selected relay is written to the normal VPN log and displayed on the Connect screen as the last relay.
+- If Smart Relay cannot find a healthy candidate, connection fails open to normal OpenConnect DNS behavior.
+- Internal broadcast/action names and FileProvider authority isolated for side-by-side testing.
+
+## Static validation completed
+
+- `git diff --check` passes.
+
+- `SmartRelaySelector.java` compiles with Java source/target 8.
+- Modified `LibOpenConnect.java` compiles with Java source/target 8.
+- Smart Relay endpoint/domain parser smoke tests pass with documentation-only examples.
+- All modified Android resource XML files parse successfully.
+- JNI integration was checked against OpenConnect 1.12's `openconnect_override_getaddrinfo()` callback contract. The callback receives the `libctx` supplied as OpenConnect cbdata, so logical-host-to-physical-IP pinning is valid by design.
+
+## Full APK build status
+
+A full APK has **not yet been produced in this sandbox** because the runtime does not contain an Android SDK/NDK or the prebuilt OpenConnect native artifacts. OpenConnect 1.12 requires Android SDK 35 / build-tools 34.0.0 and NDK r27c; this source also requires rebuilding `libopenconnect.so` because MVP1 adds one JNI method for Smart Relay.
+
+The source is ready for the native/Android build stage. The next build environment must run the upstream external dependency build and then Gradle assembleDebug.
+
+## MVP1 limitations to address after first device test
+
+- Relay selection pre-probes candidates, but does not yet automatically try the second-best relay inside the *same* authentication attempt if the selected relay dies between probe and connection. A new manual Connect attempt re-runs selection.
+- The relay pool is persistent and additive. Time-based aging/garbage collection and scored cooldown history are planned after first APK validation.
+- The Connect screen now uses a distinct dark Smart Connect visual system with live tunnel/relay IP and transfer statistics.
+- The large circular Connect/Disconnect control is deliberately positioned in the lower half directly above the fixed navigation, inside the one-handed thumb zone.
+- Servers have a dedicated card list and low, reachable selection flow. The working Smart Relay/OpenConnect backend is unchanged.
+- The launcher/QS tile icon is a new relay-path mark and does not reuse OpenConnect branding.
